From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Darrel=20Gri=C3=ABt?= <dgriet@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] asoc: msm8909: Release shared pin mux bits on shutdown
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The GPIO mux registers are shared between the MI2S ports and AUXPCM, and every
startup handler only ORs its own bits in. Nothing clears them again, so the mux
holds everything opened since boot and the speaker ends up muxed away.

The LPASS clock still enables and ASoC still reports the back end started, so
the kernel logs no error. The bit clock never reaches the TFA9895 though, which
reports CLKS=0/PLLS=0 and stops switching until the next boot:

    Startup of device [left] is a warmstart
    ERROR: SWS
    Misc errors detected: STATUS_FLAG0 = 0x1d

Enumerating the card is enough. Opening AUXPCM Hostless, Tertiary MI2S_TX
Hostless, VoLTE, VoWLAN, INT_HFP_BT Hostless or the senary capture device each
silence the speaker, so one espeak run silences the watch until reboot.

Clear the bits a path claimed once it is done with them. Bits shared with
another path stay set. There is no refcount here, and dropping one under an
active stream would be worse than leaking it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [android vendor kernel]
Signed-off-by: Darrel Griët <dgriet@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/asoc/msm8909.c b/asoc/msm8909.c
index a3706907..2e5de090 100755
--- a/asoc/msm8909.c
+++ b/asoc/msm8909.c
@@ -829,6 +829,29 @@ static int msm_mclk_event(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The GPIO mux registers are shared between the MI2S ports and AUXPCM, and
+ * every startup handler only ORs its own bits in. With no matching clear on
+ * shutdown the mux holds everything opened since boot, which leaves the
+ * speaker muxed away. The LPASS clock still enables and the kernel logs no
+ * error, but the bit clock never reaches the amplifier, so it reports
+ * CLKS=0/PLLS=0 and stops switching until the next boot.
+ *
+ * Clear the bits a path claimed once it is done with them. Bits shared with
+ * another path stay set. There is no refcount here, and dropping one under an
+ * active stream would be worse than leaking it.
+ */
+static void msm_mi2s_mux_release(void __iomem *mux, u32 bits)
+{
+	u32 val;
+
+	if (!mux)
+		return;
+
+	val = ioread32(mux);
+	iowrite32(val & ~bits, mux);
+}
+
 static int msm_mi2s_snd_startup(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 {
 	struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd = substream->private_data;
@@ -896,6 +919,8 @@ static void msm_mi2s_snd_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 	if (ret < 0)
 		pr_err("%s:clock disable failed; ret=%d\n", __func__,
 				ret);
+	msm_mi2s_mux_release(pdata->vaddr_gpio_mux_spkr_ctl, 0x00010000);
+	msm_mi2s_mux_release(pdata->vaddr_gpio_mux_mic_ctl, 0x00200000);
 	if (atomic_read(&pdata->int_mclk0_rsc_ref) > 0) {
 		atomic_dec(&pdata->int_mclk0_rsc_ref);
 		pr_debug("%s: decrementing mclk_res_ref %d\n", __func__,
@@ -965,6 +990,7 @@ static void msm_prim_auxpcm_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 		(atomic_read(&pdata->int_mclk0_rsc_ref) == 0)) {
 		msm_enable_dig_cdc_clk(codec, 0, true);
 	}
+	msm_mi2s_mux_release(pdata->vaddr_gpio_mux_pcm_ctl, 0x00000001);
 	if (pdata->mi2s_gpio_p[QUAT_MI2S]) {
 		ret =  msm_cdc_pinctrl_select_sleep_state(
 			pdata->mi2s_gpio_p[QUAT_MI2S]);
@@ -1065,6 +1091,7 @@ static void msm_sec_mi2s_snd_shutdown(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream)
 	ret = msm_mi2s_sclk_ctl(substream, false);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		pr_err("%s:clock disable failed\n", __func__);
+	msm_mi2s_mux_release(pdata->vaddr_gpio_mux_spkr_ctl, 0x0004835c);
 	}
 }
 
